{UTF-8}
Actual renewable share=MIN(1, Renewable generation / Electricity demand)
	~	
	~		|

Base CO2 price=80
	~	EUR/t
	~		|

Base gas fuel cost=60
	~	
	~		|

Cannibalisation factor=0.8
	~	
	~		|

Capacity factor=0.3
	~	Fraction
	~		|

Capacity under construction= INTEG (investment starts-completion,
		12.5 * construction time)
	~	GW
	~		|

CO2 price=Base CO2 price + STEP(CO2 step height, CO2 step time)
	~	EUR/t
	~		|

CO2 step height=0
	~	EUR/t
	~		|

CO2 step time=2035
	~	Year
	~		|

completion=Capacity under construction / construction time
	~	
	~		|

construction time=3
	~	Year
	~		|

Electricity demand=500
	~	TWh/yr
	~		|

Emission factor=0.37
	~	t/MWh
	~		|

expected market value=Gas set price * MAX(0.1, 1 - Cannibalisation factor * Share seen by investor\
		)
	~	EUR/MWh
	~		|

Gas fuel cost=Base gas fuel cost + RAMP(Gas price trend, 2025, 2060) + Gas shock height\
		 * PULSE(Gas shock time, Gas shock duration)
	~	EUR/MWh
	~		|

Gas price trend=0
	~	EUR/MWh per year
	~		|

Gas set price=Gas fuel cost + CO2 price * Emission factor
	~	EUR/MWh
	~		|

Gas shock duration=3
	~	years
	~		|

Gas shock height=50
	~	EUR/MWh
	~		|

Gas shock time=2030
	~	Year
	~		|

Generation per GW=8.76*Capacity factor
	~	TWh/yr per GW
	~		|

Initial installed capacity=50
	~	GW
	~		|

Initial LCOE=55
	~	EUR/MWh
	~		|

Installed renewable capacity= INTEG (completion-retirements,
		Initial installed capacity)
	~	GW
	~		|

investment response=1
	~	Year
	~		|

investment starts=Installed renewable capacity * MAX(0, MIN(Max growth rate, investment response\
		 * (profitability - 1)))
	~	
	~		|

Learning exponent=-LN(1 - learning rate) / LN(2)
	~	dimensionless
	~		|

learning rate=0.15
	~	Fraction
	~		|

Max growth rate=0.25
	~	Year
	~		|

Perceived market value=SMOOTH(expected market value, Perception time)
	~	
	~		|

Perception time=1
	~	Year
	~		|

Plant lifetime=25
	~	
	~		|

profitability=Perceived market value / Renewable LCOE
	~	ratio
	~		|

Renewable generation=Installed renewable capacity * Generation per GW
	~	TWh/yr
	~		|

Renewable LCOE=Initial LCOE * (Installed renewable capacity / Initial installed capacity\
		) ^ (-Learning exponent)
	~	{Initial LCOE * (Installed renewable capacity / Initial installed capacity) ^ (-Learning exponent)}
	~		|

retirements=Installed renewable capacity / Plant lifetime
	~	GW/yr
	~		|

Share seen by investor=MIN(1, (Installed renewable capacity + Supply line weight * Capacity under construction\
		) * Generation per GW
	 / Electricity demand)
	~	
	~		|

Supply line weight=0
	~	
	~		|

********************************************************
	.Control
********************************************************~
		Simulation Control Parameters
	|

FINAL TIME  = 2060
	~	Year
	~	The final time for the simulation.
	|

INITIAL TIME  = 2025
	~	Year
	~	The initial time for the simulation.
	|

SAVEPER  = 
        TIME STEP 
	~	Year [0,?]
	~	The frequency with which output is stored.
	|

TIME STEP  = 0.019231
	~	Year [0,?]
	~	The time step for the simulation.
	|

